  "result": "```json\n{\n    \"smpl.ordering.controllers.CatalogController\": {\n        \"summary\": \"REST controller that manages catalog items in an ordering system. Provides CRUD operations for catalog items through HTTP endpoints mapped to /catalog. Key methods include: getCatalogItems() (GET /catalog) to retrieve all catalog items; getCatalogItem(String sku) (GET /catalog/{sku}) to retrieve a specific item by SKU number; addCatalogItem(CatalogItem info) (POST /catalog) to create new catalog items with validation and conflict checking; upsertCatalogItem(String sku, CatalogItem info) (PUT /catalog/{sku}) to update existing items; and removeCatalogItem(String sku) (DELETE /catalog/{sku}) to remove items. The controller integrates with Application Insights for telemetry tracking, validates all input data before processing, returns appropriate HTTP status codes (200 OK, 201 CREATED, 204 NO_CONTENT, 400 BAD_REQUEST, 404 NOT_FOUND, 409 CONFLICT, 500 INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR), and uses the repository pattern through CatalogItemsRepository to abstract data access operations. Exception handling is implemented across all endpoints with telemetry tracking for monitoring and debugging purposes.\",\n        \"file_path\": \"smpl/ordering/controllers/CatalogController.java\"\n    }\n}\n```",
